course: dictionary
lesson: 8467
title: Salmonella: tiny germs, big tummy trouble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Salmonella is a kind of bacteria. Bacteria are tiny living things, too small to see, and some of them can make us ill. When people say salmonella, they can mean the bacteria or the illness they cause, which is also called food poisoning.
explain: Use the clues in the sentences. «Children in Ohio cuddled and kissed backyard chickens; several got Salmonella and were sick for days.» The clues are got, sick and days, so salmonella is something that makes you ill for a long time. Swap in your meaning to check: "several got food poisoning and were sick for days" still makes sense.
explain: Salmonella can be found in raw chicken, raw eggs, unwashed food, and on reptiles like turtles and lizards. «Reptiles often carry salmonella germs, so you wash your hands with soap after every touch.» The clue is the word so: the washing is the answer to the germs.
fact: Salmonella is a kind of bacteria that can cause food poisoning.
fact: Symptoms include stomach ache, being sick, diarrhoea and fever.
fact: Salmonella can be found in raw chicken, raw eggs, unwashed food, and on reptiles such as turtles, snakes and lizards.
fact: To stay safe, wash your hands, keep raw meat apart from ready-to-eat food, cook chicken and eggs fully, and don't eat raw cake mix.
exercise: «Reptiles often carry salmonella germs, so you wash your hands with soap after every touch.» What is the safest thing to do after touching a reptile? | Give the reptile a kiss | *Wash your hands with soap | Eat a snack straight away | Leave your hands dirty for later
exercise: Salmonella is a kind of bacteria. What are bacteria? | Bits of food left on a plate | Kinds of medicine | *Tiny living things, too small to see | Large animals that live in the sea
exercise: «Chickens can carry salmonella germs, so you wash your hands after handling them or their eggs.» Which food must be cooked fully to stay safe? | *Chicken and eggs | Cold orange juice | Bread from the shop | Fresh apples
test: «Turtles, tortoises, lizards, snakes and baby chicks often carry salmonella germs.» Which animal is NOT in this list? | Lizard | Baby chick | Turtle | *Cat
test: Why should you not eat raw cake mix? | *It can contain salmonella germs that make you ill | Because it is too cold to eat | Because it tastes bitter | To keep your teeth clean
exam: Which two actions help stop salmonella spreading? | Touching turtles and not washing | *Washing hands and keeping raw meat apart from ready-to-eat food | Keeping food warm on the table for a week | Eating raw eggs and leaving meat out all day
